Third-party code and ideas
--------------------------

SkyCraft by chasmlol (https://github.com/chasmlol/SkyCraft)
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 chasmlol.
  The Minecraft side of Portalcraft (bridge/fabric) is derived from SkyCraft's
  Fabric mod, and the architecture (a host-game plugin drawing Minecraft's own
  meshes, fed over shared memory by a hidden Minecraft with a Fabric mod)
  follows it. The licence text is bridge/fabric/LICENSE-SkyCraft and is
  shipped inside the mod jar.

SourceAutoRecord by the p2sr contributors (https://github.com/p2sr/SourceAutoRecord)
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2021 The SAR authors.
  bridge/src/sar is a trimmed fork of its plugin framework (interface lookup,
  signature scanning, hooks, the "Portal 2 10090" offset tables).
  Licence text: bridge/src/sar/LICENSE-SourceAutoRecord.

LodePNG 20120729 by Lode Vandevenne (as carried in SourceAutoRecord)
  zlib licence, Copyright (c) 2005-2012 Lode Vandevenne.
  bridge/src/sar/Utils/lodepng.*; the licence text is in the file headers.

Create by The Creators of Create (https://github.com/Creators-of-Create/Create)
  MIT License, Copyright (c) The Create Team / The Creators of Create (code
  only; no assets are used).
  The collision of moving structures in bridge/fabric/.../world/SkyMovers.java
  is adapted from Create's ContraptionCollider / ContinuousOBBCollider.
  Licence text: bridge/fabric/LICENSE-Create, shipped inside the mod jar.

Immersive Portals by qouteall (https://github.com/iPortalTeam/ImmersivePortalsMod)
  Apache License 2.0. Approach only, no code copied: the idea of which player
  fields must move with the player through a portal, and the rendering
  approach for portal views.

Libraries downloaded at build or run time and not redistributed here: Fabric
Loader, Fabric API and Fabric Loom (Apache-2.0 and the Fabric licences),
Gradle (Apache-2.0).


